<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sila Region</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sila is a region of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, on the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, with its capital at Goz Beïda. It corresponds to the old sultanate of Dar Sila, ruled by a dynasty related to that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> from about the 17th century until the 20th. The region was created in 2008 and has hosted large numbers of refugees and displaced people from the conflicts in Darfur and eastern Chad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sila-region.jpg" alt="Sila Region" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sombo Ario · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goz-Be%C3%AFda,_Sila_,Tchad_Est.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
